mphocyte count reduction appears more prevalent in longer treatment durations. While the clinical significance of mild lymphocytopenia in HCV therapy remains context-dependent, persistent or severe reductions could indicate immunosuppression or other underlying issues, necessitating periodic complete blood count assessments [Data: Entities (16414); Relationships (15133)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"鼻咽炎 is among the most common mild clinical side effects\",\n            \"explanation\": \"鼻咽炎 (nasopharyngitis) is reported in 10% of patients receiving 索磷布韦/维帕他韦, making it one of the top four most frequent non-serious adverse events. Described as generally mild and not requiring specific treatment, this upper respiratory symptom aligns with the drug’s overall safety profile. Its inclusion highlights that while SOF/VEL is well-tolerated, common viral-like symptoms may still occur during therapy [Data: Entities (17802); Relationships (15136)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Potential interaction with antihypertensive drugs requires clinical monitoring\",\n            \"explanation\": \"索磷布韦/维帕他韦 may interact with certain antihypertensive agents, such as amlodipine, potentially affecting blood pressure control. Pharmacists recommend enhanced clinical monitoring—including blood pressure follow-up—when these drugs are co-administered. Although the exact mechanism is not fully elucidated, this relationship signals the need for caution in patients with comorbid hypertension, especially given the high prevalence of cardiovascular conditions in some HCV populations [Data: Relationships (3823)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Contraindications exist with specific antiarrhythmic and CNS drugs\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Although not directly part of the listed entities, supporting evidence within relationship record 3823 notes that 索磷布韦/维帕他韦-containing regimens are contraindicated with amiodarone due to 